Port provenance and attribution
===============================

This distribution packages a third-party port ("BENI velocity-flat for
MotrixLab"). All ported material keeps its upstream provenance:

1. BENI robot description (MJCF, meshes, textures), reward structure,
   observation/action layout, and the passive knee spring model originate
   from:
       Mondo-Robotics/open-beni
       https://github.com/Mondo-Robotics/open-beni
       Copyright (c) 2026 Open Beni
       SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
   Individual ported files carry their own header notices where practical.

2. The adaptation targets MotrixLab by Motphys Technology:
       https://github.com/Motphys/MotrixLab
       Apache License 2.0
   This distribution contains no MotrixLab source files; it adds new
   robot/task modules through MotrixLab's extension points and appends two
   import lines to registration __init__.py files during installation.

3. Trained policy checkpoints in overlay/runs/ were produced with this port
   on public hardware; they are distributed under the same MIT license as
   the port. They embed no third-party weights beyond this project's own
   training run.

4. The linearized knee spring constants were derived by least-squares fit of
   the upstream nonlinear spring curve over the knee's standing range.

If you redistribute, keep this NOTICE, the LICENSE, and the upstream
copyright headers in ported source files.
